leandvb (leansdr work 84c59e1) DVB-S2 acquisition fixes; applies after leandvb-ldpc-helper.patch.

1. The PLHEADER search window covered MIN_SYMBOLS_PER_FRAME, 39 % of a normal QPSK frame: often it held no PLHEADER and
   the best correlation was in the data, a false lock (MER -12..-15 dB) that could last many seconds. With normal
   frames allowed it now covers the longest frame.
2. The first frame's PLSCODE was decoded from LLRs with only the rough frequency of the differential correlator; a
   ~180 deg rotation across the PLHEADER turns a code into the one that differs in its second half (QPSK 3/5 -> 1/2,
   5/6 -> 4/5), and the lock then kept a carrier off by whole cycles between pilots: those MODCODs never decoded.
   Now every allowed code gets its own frequency/phase/amplitude fit and the best MER wins (a fit more than Rs/16
   away from the LLR candidate's is skipped: the PILOTS bit looks like a shift of Rs/2).
3. A first PLHEADER more than 6 dB below its MODCOD's Es/N0 is not locked on.

